    // ---------------------------------------------------------------
    // The combined insert-and-copy command alphabet (704 symbols) -
    // each symbol decomposes, via this fixed static table, into an
    // insert-length code and a copy-length code (each contributing its
    // own extra-bit count and base offset), plus a "distance context"
    // (0-3, based on the command's own copy length - already baked
    // into the table rather than recomputed) and an "implied distance
    // code" marker (`-1` meaning "read a real distance from the
    // bitstream", `0` meaning one of the two special zero-extra-bits
    // shortest commands that always reuse the *last* used distance
